Based on the context provided, when a streaming resume attempt fails with HTTP 409 (checkpoint mismatch), the server's error payload includes a structured error frame with the following JSON schema:

```json
{
  "title": "Streaming Error",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "status": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "Error status code",
      "enum": [400, 409]],
    "message": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Error message"
    },
    "resume_details": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Additional resume details",
      "properties": {
        "checkpoint_cursor": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Cursor pointing to the last successful checkpoint"
        },
        "last_successful_checkpoint": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "The last successful checkpoint",
          "properties": {
            "schema_version": {
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "The schema version of the last successful checkpoint"
            },
            "data": {
              "type": "object",
              "description": "The data contained in the last successful checkpoint"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The `kv_crc` value inside v2 resume tokens is computed as a cyclic redundancy check (CRC) of the key-value pair represented by the resume token. The CRC algorithm used is the 32-bit CRC
